  <ferc:DisclosureOfImportantNotesRegardingFinancialStatementsTextBlock id="f-19" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;Basis of Accounting&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;DCP Sand Hills Pipeline, LLC is subject to regulation by the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission (FERC). The accounting policies followed in preparation of these financial statements generally conform to those required by FERC.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;DCP Sand Hills Pipeline, LLC, or the owner, funds the operations of Sand Hills. As Sand Hills has no cash accounts, all of cash management activity is performed by the owner and affiliates on Sand Hills&#8217; behalf, including collection of receivables, payment of payables, and the settlement of sales and purchases transactions. Net amounts due to or from Sand Hills to or from the owner or affiliates are settled periodically by the transfer of such receivables and payables to the owner or affiliates and are shown as net contributions or distributions in equity&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfImportantNotesRegardingFinancialStatementsTextBlock>
